pothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa,\\mathcal L,\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{fn}},\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{const}},a,\\mathcal A,\\mathcal B\\in V\">\\(\\kappa,\\mathcal L,\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{fn}},\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{const}},a,\\mathcal A,\\mathcal B\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\\)</span> (cardinal predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L=\\langle\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{fn}},\\varnothing,\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{const}},a\\rangle\">\\(\\mathcal L=\\langle\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{fn}},\\varnothing,\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{const}},a\\rangle\\)</span> (countable functional first-order language)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Language}_S,\\mathrm{Struct}_S,\\mathrm{Substructure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Language}_S,\\mathrm{Struct}_S,\\mathrm{Substructure}_S\\)</span> (language and structure predicates)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcCard6CountableSet}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcCard6CountableSet}_S\\)</span> (countable-set predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Jonsson}\">\\(\\operatorname{Jonsson}\\)</span> (Jónsson-cardinal predicate)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}jonsson\\text{-}cardinal}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{Jonsson}(\\kappa)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\omega&lt;\\kappa\n\\land\\forall\\mathcal L,\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{fn}},\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{const}},a\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Language}_S(\\mathcal L,\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{fn}},\\varnothing,\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{const}},a)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcCard6CountableSet}_S(\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{fn}}\\cup\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{const}})\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{25mm}\\to\\forall\\mathcal A\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Struct}_S(\\mathcal A,\\mathcal L)\\land|\\operatorname{Univ}(\\mathcal A)|=\\kappa\n\\to\\exists\\mathcal B\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Substructure}_S(\\mathcal B,\\mathcal A,\\mathcal L)\n\\land\\operatorname{Univ}(\\mathcal B)\\subsetneq\\operatorname{Univ}(\\mathcal A)\n\\land|\\operatorname{Univ}(\\mathcal B)|=\\kappa\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}jonsson\\text{-}cardinal}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{Jonsson}(\\kappa)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\omega&lt;\\kappa\n\\land\\forall\\mathcal L,\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{fn}},\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{const}},a\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Language}_S(\\mathcal L,\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{fn}},\\varnothing,\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{const}},a)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcCard6CountableSet}_S(\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{fn}}\\cup\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{const}})\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{25mm}\\to\\forall\\mathcal A\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Struct}_S(\\mathcal A,\\mathcal L)\\land|\\operatorname{Univ}(\\mathcal A)|=\\kappa\n\\to\\exists\\mathcal B\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Substructure}_S(\\mathcal B,\\mathcal A,\\mathcal L)\n\\land\\operatorname{Univ}(\\mathcal B)\\subsetneq\\operatorname{Univ}(\\mathcal A)\n\\land|\\operatorname{Univ}(\\mathcal B)|=\\kappa\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Equivalently, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\\to[\\kappa]^{&lt;\\omega}_\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\to[\\kappa]^{&lt;\\omega}_\\kappa\\)</span>: every coloring of the finite subsets of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> into <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> colors omits a color on some subset of size <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>It is open whether <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\aleph_\\omega\">\\(\\aleph_\\omega\\)</span> is Jónsson; if it is, it is the least possible Jónsson cardinal. 